# Line endings are the checkout's business — except for the files whose *content*
# the app parses, where they are the product's.
#
# `docs/*.md` and the changelogs are bundled with Vite `?raw` and split line by
# line at runtime (`lib/appInfo/docOutline.ts`, `changelog.ts`,
# `components/shell/Markdown.tsx`). With `core.autocrlf=true` — the default on a
# Windows clone — those imports carried CRLF, so the app's behaviour differed
# between a Windows dev machine and CI, and the docs-outline round-trip test
# failed on the former only. Pinning markdown to LF makes the three
# `replace(/\r\n/g, "\n")` calls belt and braces instead of load-bearing.
#
# Everything else keeps git's normal auto-detection: source files may be CRLF in
# a Windows working copy, as they are today.
* text=auto
*.md text eol=lf
